  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Consider an infinite geometric series with first term $a$ and common ratio $r$. If its sum is 4 and the second term is $\\frac{3}{4}$, then:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "pDgYW",
      "text": "$a=\\frac{4}{7}, r=\\frac{3}{7}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "g9aNQ",
      "text": "$a=2, r=\\frac{3}{8}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "vpTaQ",
      "text": "$a=\\frac{3}{2}, r=\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "w9ylZ",
      "text": "$a=3, r=\\frac{1}{4}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since, sum $=4$ and second term $=\\frac{3}{4}$ $\\Rightarrow \\frac{a}{1-r}=4$, and $a r=\\frac{3}{4}$ $\\Rightarrow \\frac{a}{1-\\frac{3}{4 a}}=4$ $\\Rightarrow(a-1)(a-3)=0$ $\\Rightarrow a=1$ or $a=3$\r\n\r\n$\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow \\frac{a}{1-\\frac{3}{4 a}}=4 \\\\\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow(a-1)(a-3)=0 \\\\\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow a=1 \\text { or } a=3\r\n\r\n\\end{array}$",
    "image": null
  },
